Z||000006||fiero56||05-01-2000||02:38 PM||||It is illegal to have the front plate off your car here in Ohio too. My front license plate and frame "fell off" my Formula in April last year. I don't like the way it looks on there, so I won't put it on there. I have driven 20,000 trouble free miles with it off. Haven't had a cop give it a second look. William Thorn III did suggest I carry the front plate under the seat in case I do get stopped though. I might do that. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||mshill||05-01-2000||05:03 PM||||Also illegal here in California, but I don't have a holder and the license plate is up in the lower front window on the passenger side held up with two little suction cup thingies.  Haven't had a problem yet... (knock on wood).||||reg||12
Z||000008||theogre||05-01-2000||07:45 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> DE is front plate free  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>I'd definatly keep it in the car, and not burried either. That way you can quickly show that you at least have the thing. ""Gee it was falling off at work so I put it ______ so I wouldn't lose it."" The bracket of course has to look like it was cracked or rusted enough to do so....... (Used to live in NY.)||||reg||1
